From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:10:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: mailbox: Do not sleep past free FIFO space

A sleeping sender that finds the send FIFO full waits on tx_empty for
the send-empty interrupt, and gives up after 500 ms. Two things make it
miss free space and time out with room in the FIFO:

- The interrupt reports an empty FIFO. A firmware that takes some of
  the queued messages but not all of them frees space without raising
  it.
- Two senders can wait at once, for example a driver starting its
  endpoints while the RTKit work item acknowledges a syslog message.
  The handler masks the interrupt and calls complete(), which wakes
  only one of them. The other sleeps on with the interrupt masked. A
  sender that timed out also masked it, stranding any sender still
  waiting.

On the J616s (M4 Pro) this delayed the AOP start on some warm boots.

Wake every waiting sender with complete_all(), and check the FIFO again
every 2 ms while waiting, until one 500 ms deadline per send. A woken
sender that still finds the FIFO full rearms the interrupt before it
waits, as before. A sender that times out now leaves the interrupt
unmasked for the others. tx_irq_unmasked still records the state, so
the enable stays balanced: the handler masks it when it fires, and
provider removal masks it otherwise. Atomic senders, which poll, are
unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(backported from commit a149ba924449885e01d540ddcf9da5633b7b6f64)
[j604: backported onto the linux-aurora 1.607 mailbox.c, which has no
 G17 paths, no ASCWrap v6 and no aurora-wip "TX wait failed" report:
 the 500 ms limit becomes one absolute deadline per send (the base
 waited up to 500 ms per wait); the rest as upstream (master 23827fe87f)]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c       | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 include/linux/soc/apple/mailbox.h |  4 +--
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c b/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
index 7ffe2b1367..2c5a90e703 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
@@ -112,6 +112,11 @@ static_assert(APPLE_ASCWRAP_V6_MBOX_OFFSET + APPLE_ASC_MBOX_I2A_RECV0 ==
 #define APPLE_MBOX_MSG1_MSG GENMASK(31, 0)
 
 #define APPLE_MBOX_TX_TIMEOUT 500
+/*
+ * The send-empty interrupt reports an empty FIFO, not free space. A sender
+ * that waits for it also checks the FIFO this often.
+ */
+#define APPLE_MBOX_TX_RECHECK_MS 2
 
 struct apple_mbox_hw {
 	unsigned int reg_offset;
@@ -270,6 +275,8 @@ int apple_mbox_send(struct apple_mbox *mbox, const struct apple_mbox_msg msg,
 		    bool atomic)
 {
 	unsigned long flags;
+	unsigned long deadline = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(APPLE_MBOX_TX_TIMEOUT);
+	unsigned long now, remaining;
 	int ret;
 	u32 mbox_ctrl;
 	long t;
@@ -282,6 +289,12 @@ int apple_mbox_send(struct apple_mbox *mbox, const struct apple_mbox_msg msg,
 	mbox_ctrl = readl_relaxed(mbox->regs + mbox->hw->a2i_control);
 
 	while (mbox_ctrl & mbox->hw->control_full) {
+		now = jiffies;
+		if (time_after_eq(now, deadline)) {
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mbox->tx_lock, flags);
+			return -ETIMEDOUT;
+		}
+		remaining = deadline - now;
 		if (atomic || mbox->irq_send_empty < 0) {
 			ret = readl_poll_timeout_atomic(
 				mbox->regs + mbox->hw->a2i_control, mbox_ctrl,
@@ -315,19 +328,19 @@ int apple_mbox_send(struct apple_mbox *mbox, const struct apple_mbox_msg msg,
 		}
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mbox->tx_lock, flags);
 
+		/*
+		 * The firmware can take messages without emptying the FIFO,
+		 * which raises no interrupt, so check it again after a short
+		 * wait; the deadline above ends the loop. Other senders may be
+		 * waiting on the same interrupt: a sender that gives up leaves
+		 * it unmasked for them. The handler masks it when it fires,
+		 * and removal masks it otherwise.
+		 */
 		t = wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(
 			&mbox->tx_empty,
-			msecs_to_jiffies(APPLE_MBOX_TX_TIMEOUT));
-		if (t <= 0) {
-			/* A late IRQ may already have masked this under tx_lock. */
-			spin_lock_irqsave(&mbox->tx_lock, flags);
-			if (mbox->tx_irq_unmasked) {
-				disable_irq_nosync(mbox->irq_send_empty);
-				mbox->tx_irq_unmasked = false;
-			}
-			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mbox->tx_lock, flags);
-			return t < 0 ? t : -ETIMEDOUT;
-		}
+			min(remaining, msecs_to_jiffies(APPLE_MBOX_TX_RECHECK_MS)));
+		if (t < 0)
+			return t;
 
 		spin_lock_irqsave(&mbox->tx_lock, flags);
 		if (unlikely(READ_ONCE(mbox->removing))) {
@@ -363,7 +376,13 @@ static irqreturn_t apple_mbox_send_empty_irq(int irq, void *data)
 		disable_irq_nosync(mbox->irq_send_empty);
 		mbox->tx_irq_unmasked = false;
 	}
-	complete(&mbox->tx_empty);
+	/*
+	 * Wake every waiting sender, not just one. The interrupt is now
+	 * masked, so a sender left asleep would only wake at its timeout,
+	 * with room in the FIFO. A woken sender that still finds the FIFO
+	 * full rearms the interrupt before it waits again.
+	 */
+	complete_all(&mbox->tx_empty);
 	spin_unlock(&mbox->tx_lock);
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
diff --git a/include/linux/soc/apple/mailbox.h b/include/linux/soc/apple/mailbox.h
index 6cbf100d03..6877b575f4 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/apple/mailbox.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/apple/mailbox.h
@@ -81,8 +81,8 @@ struct apple_mbox {
 
 	/*
 	 * Protected by tx_lock: set while irq_send_empty is unmasked, so that
-	 * the IRQ handler, a failed send and provider removal mask it exactly
-	 * once between them.
+	 * the IRQ handler and provider removal mask it exactly once between
+	 * them.
 	 */
 	bool tx_irq_unmasked;
 };
